WEBVTT

00:02.810 --> 00:05.600
<b><i>Sanosuke Sagara, age 19.</i></b>

00:03.230 --> 00:14.490
<b>BAD</b>

00:06.150 --> 00:10.110
<b><i>Born in 1860 as the oldest son
of a farmer in Shinshu.</i></b>

00:10.610 --> 00:14.490
<b><i>Basically ran away from home to join
the Sekiho Army at the age of nine.</i></b>

00:15.160 --> 00:18.330
<b><i>Considers and admires their Captain,
Sozo Sagara as his master.</i></b>

00:18.830 --> 00:21.080
<b><i>But the group was given
the disgraceful title</i></b>

00:21.080 --> 00:23.080
<b><i>of fake Imperial Army,
and Sozo was beheaded.</i></b>

00:23.250 --> 00:25.420
<b><i>That led to the collapse
of the Sekiho Army.</i></b>

00:26.290 --> 00:30.250
<b><i>He then moved to Tokyo, where he
became a fighter for hire called Zanza.</i></b>

00:30.250 --> 00:32.210
<b><i>He became infamous
in underground society,</i></b>

00:32.210 --> 00:35.680
<b><i>but he then faced defeat
from the rurouni Kenshin Himura.</i></b>

00:36.180 --> 00:39.010
<b><i>Since his defeat,
he often heads over to Kamiya Dojo,</i></b>

00:39.010 --> 00:42.640
<b><i>and he is currently leading
a leisurely life as a vagabond.</i></b>

00:42.640 --> 00:43.520
<b>Huh?</b>

02:15.990 --> 02:19.990
<b>EPISODE 18:
SANOSUKE &
NISHIKI PAINTINGS</b>

02:19.990 --> 02:22.160
<b>BEEF HOT-POT AND SAKE
AKABEKO RESTAURANT</b>

02:20.910 --> 02:22.160
<b>Nishiki paintings?</b>

02:22.410 --> 02:25.040
<b>There's a new shipment today.</b>

02:25.540 --> 02:30.710
<b>But it's drawn by a popular artist,
so it sells out quickly.</b>

02:31.080 --> 02:34.840
<b>And I just can't leave work
at all today.</b>

02:35.050 --> 02:38.300
<b>So you want me to go buy it for you.</b>

02:38.300 --> 02:40.720
<b>Yes. Can I ask that of you?</b>

02:40.970 --> 02:42.340
<b>You can ask Yahiko—</b>

02:42.550 --> 02:45.100
<b>I'm working, too, you idiot!</b>

02:45.310 --> 02:48.060
<b>Sheesh! This is why vagabonds are...</b>

02:49.390 --> 02:52.270
<b>Oh, well.
I guess I can run errands for you.</b>

02:52.770 --> 02:55.150
<b>You do give me free meals
all the time, after all.</b>

02:55.150 --> 02:57.110
<b>They aren't free meals.</b>

02:57.110 --> 02:59.490
<b>Everything you've eaten 'til now
is still on a tab.</b>

02:59.490 --> 03:01.610
<b>Don't worry about the details.</b>

03:01.820 --> 03:04.990
<b>So, what art
from which artist do you want?</b>

03:04.990 --> 03:08.950
<b>"Swordsman Hachiro Iba"
by Tsunan Tsukioka!</b>

03:08.950 --> 03:12.080
<b>Oh, the handsome swordsman,
the most popular of the Bakumatsu Era.</b>

03:12.080 --> 03:14.000
<b>"One-Arm Iba-Hachi," huh?</b>

03:15.710 --> 03:16.960
<b>U-Um...</b>

03:16.960 --> 03:17.840
<b>Huh?</b>

03:20.050 --> 03:22.300
<b>Oh, no. It's nothing.</b>

03:22.800 --> 03:27.260
<b>You should clearly say what you
want to say. Got that, little girl?</b>

03:27.770 --> 03:28.770
<b>No...</b>

03:29.520 --> 03:30.350
<b>I see.</b>

03:31.350 --> 03:35.730
<b>So two copies of Iba-Hachi
by Tsunan Tsukioka, yeah?</b>

03:37.360 --> 03:40.360
<b>Gotta hand it to Sano.
He's really the man.</b>

03:40.570 --> 03:44.740
<b>Really. Now only
if he would pay up properly.</b>

03:45.870 --> 03:49.160
<b>But, you know,
a mellowed-out Sano is great and all,</b>

03:49.160 --> 03:51.870
<b>but how he used to be
was pretty awesome, too.</b>

03:51.870 --> 03:53.620
<b>Yeah. Zanza!</b>

03:54.000 --> 03:59.460
<b>He would be smiling, but he wasn't
satisfied at the bottom of his heart.</b>

03:59.880 --> 04:03.340
<b>It was like a bomb
that was about to go off.</b>

04:04.300 --> 04:06.300
<b>He was always glaring.</b>

04:11.020 --> 04:12.430
<b><i>Nishiki paintings.</i></b>

04:12.430 --> 04:15.980
<b><i>Back during the Edo period,
actors and scenery were the convention.</i></b>

04:16.480 --> 04:20.110
<b><i>But once the Meiji Era rolled around,
many other things were drawn as well,</i></b>

04:20.530 --> 04:22.860
<b><i>making it more generalized
in pop culture.</i></b>

04:23.700 --> 04:26.870
<b><i>In the modern day,
they serve as important references</i></b>

04:27.240 --> 04:29.410
<b><i>that convey Meiji culture and customs.</i></b>

04:29.410 --> 04:30.330
<b>Hmm?</b>

04:30.580 --> 04:31.700
<b>Welcome.</b>

04:31.700 --> 04:32.710
<b>Hey.</b>

04:33.210 --> 04:34.040
<b>Sano?</b>

04:34.960 --> 04:36.670
<b>Hey, both of you.</b>

04:36.670 --> 04:38.710
<b>Nishiki paintings, that is?</b>

04:38.710 --> 04:40.420
<b>This is unusual, that it is.</b>

04:40.880 --> 04:42.760
<b>Perhaps one of a beautiful lady?</b>

04:42.760 --> 04:43.760
<b>Nope.</b>

04:43.760 --> 04:45.380
<b>Perhaps an erotic one?</b>

04:45.380 --> 04:46.390
<b>Oh, my...</b>

04:46.390 --> 04:48.260
<b>Of course not.</b>

04:48.470 --> 04:50.720
<b>Tae at Akabeko asked me to get one.</b>

04:51.220 --> 04:52.470
<b>It ain't for me.</b>

04:53.100 --> 04:56.850
<b>Mister, you got two more copies
of Tsunan Tsukioka's Iba-Hachi?</b>

04:56.850 --> 05:01.570
<b>HACHIRO HIDESATO IBA</b>

04:56.850 --> 05:02.230
<b>You're in luck, sir.
Those are the last two I've got.</b>

05:02.230 --> 05:06.030
<b>Tsunan's art is really popular,
so they sell out real quick.</b>

05:06.320 --> 05:08.120
<b>Those two total 10 sen.</b>

05:08.620 --> 05:10.450
<b>Oh, I don't have any money.</b>

05:10.950 --> 05:12.200
<b>Can you lend me some?</b>

05:12.200 --> 05:13.330
<b>Sheesh!</b>

05:13.330 --> 05:16.420
<b>HIJIKATA</b>

05:13.330 --> 05:16.500
<b>That said,
you call 'em all Nishiki paintings,</b>

05:13.330 --> 05:20.130
<b>SHINOBAZU-NO-IKE</b>

05:13.330 --> 05:21.800
<b>YOKOZUNA</b>

05:16.500 --> 05:18.040
<b>but there sure are many kinds.</b>

05:18.040 --> 05:20.170
<b>Looks like there are
a lot from the Bakumatsu Era</b>

05:20.170 --> 05:21.880
<b>and the Revolution, too, that there are.</b>

05:21.800 --> 05:26.760
<b>A CERTAIN SAIGO AND HIS DOG</b>

05:21.880 --> 05:25.260
<b>That's right. Those of Revolutionary
warriors and Imperial Army folks</b>

05:25.260 --> 05:27.800
<b>sell well as souvenirs from Tokyo.</b>

05:27.800 --> 05:31.680
<b>Shogunate guys like Iba-Hachi
are popular among the Edo locals.</b>

05:29.220 --> 05:31.680
<b>SHINOBAZU-NO-IKE</b>

05:33.060 --> 05:36.310
<b>SEKIHO ARMY CAPTAIN
SOZO SAGARA</b>

05:34.020 --> 05:35.020
<b>Sano?</b>

05:35.020 --> 05:36.310
<b>This is...</b>

05:36.310 --> 05:38.150
<b>SOZO</b>

05:36.390 --> 05:38.150
<b>Captain Sagara.</b>

05:39.310 --> 05:44.820
<b>Oh, that? It's also drawn by Tsunan,
but that one just doesn't sell at all.</b>

05:44.820 --> 05:49.780
<b>SEKIHO ARMY CAPTAIN
SOZO SAGARA</b>

05:45.030 --> 05:49.780
<b>But he always draws that guy, even though
he's the boss of the fake Imperial Army.</b>

05:52.740 --> 05:54.540
<b>Tsunan Tsukioka...</b>

05:55.500 --> 05:56.870
<b>Tsukioka...</b>

06:00.210 --> 06:02.340
<b>Where is this guy?</b>

06:02.630 --> 06:03.800
<b>Huh?</b>

06:04.170 --> 06:06.550
<b>Where is this Tsunan guy at?</b>

06:06.550 --> 06:07.510
<b>Sano!</b>

06:07.510 --> 06:10.550
<b>Th-The next town over
in the Dobuita Nagaya!</b>

06:10.550 --> 06:11.930
<b>But that guy sure hates people,</b>

06:11.930 --> 06:15.310
<b>so you most likely
won't be able to see him even if you go.</b>

06:16.310 --> 06:17.180
<b>Oh, I will.</b>

06:19.400 --> 06:21.940
<b>There's no way he'd refuse to see me.</b>

06:27.070 --> 06:28.280
<b>TSUKIOKA</b>

06:28.280 --> 06:30.660
<b>Mr. Tsukioka. Mr. Tsukioka.</b>

06:31.160 --> 06:32.990
<b>So you're not around, Mr. Tsukioka?</b>

06:35.870 --> 06:37.200
<b>I know you're in there,</b>

06:37.200 --> 06:40.960
<b>ex-Sekiho Army associate member,
Katsuhiro Tsukioka!</b>

06:44.090 --> 06:45.090
<b>I knew it.</b>

06:45.090 --> 06:48.010
<b>SEKIHO ARMY CAPTAIN
SOZO SAGARA</b>

06:45.920 --> 06:47.920
<b>So you really did draw this.</b>

06:49.090 --> 06:50.090
<b>Sanosuke?</b>

06:50.590 --> 06:53.350
<b>How did you...</b>

06:53.350 --> 06:56.020
<b>It was obvious when I saw this.
Right next to the captain...</b>

06:56.020 --> 06:59.810
<b>there's your old self, as well as me.</b>

07:00.770 --> 07:03.400
<b>There's no other guy out there
that would draw this.</b>

07:06.650 --> 07:07.650
<b>I see.</b>

07:07.940 --> 07:11.490
<b>So the artist Tsunan Tsukioka was also
a surviving member of the Sekiho Army.</b>

07:11.990 --> 07:13.870
<b>Let's go home, Miss Kaoru.</b>

07:14.370 --> 07:18.330
<b>Sano was acting very strangely,
so we decided to follow him,</b>

07:18.330 --> 07:20.080
<b>but there aren't any real issues on hand.</b>

07:20.290 --> 07:24.290
<b>And as that one word "bad" shows,</b>

07:24.290 --> 07:27.090
<b>the Sekiho Army
is a special memory for Sano.</b>

07:27.800 --> 07:31.220
<b>Outsiders are unwanted
in the world of memories, that they are.</b>

07:40.180 --> 07:41.060
<b>But still...</b>

07:41.270 --> 07:44.060
<b>I didn't think you'd end up an artist.</b>

07:44.310 --> 07:47.320
<b>Come to think of it,
you always were skillful.</b>

07:47.320 --> 07:50.990
<b>Whether it be hard-to-handle guns
or blending gunpowder,</b>

07:50.990 --> 07:52.700
<b>you handled things so easily.</b>

07:53.200 --> 07:55.950
<b>And so, what exactly do you do nowadays?</b>

07:56.450 --> 07:59.250
<b>Nothing. Just an old vagabond.</b>

07:59.250 --> 08:01.370
<b>I'm having fun in my own way.</b>

08:04.000 --> 08:05.080
<b>I see.</b>

08:06.500 --> 08:08.550
<b>So you are having a fun life.</b>

08:10.260 --> 08:14.390
<b>I haven't experienced any fun at all
in the past 10 years.</b>

08:15.390 --> 08:18.010
<b>I spent the last 10 years
holding a grudge against those</b>

08:18.010 --> 08:22.390
<b>that tarnished the name of Captain Sagara
and us in the Sekiho Army.</b>

08:23.980 --> 08:27.980
<b>You've gotten even more glum
than 10 years ago.</b>

08:28.480 --> 08:30.990
<b>You still don't have any friends at all?</b>

08:31.820 --> 08:35.570
<b>But, well,
I know that feeling all too well.</b>

08:39.160 --> 08:43.870
<b>I didn't think I'd reunite with you on
the day when I finished all preparations.</b>

08:44.830 --> 08:49.800
<b>Maybe this is the guidance
of our captain from up in heaven.</b>

08:50.550 --> 08:51.420
<b>Katsu?</b>

08:51.920 --> 08:56.300
<b>Sanosuke, why don't you and I
recreate the Sekiho Army once again?</b>

08:57.930 --> 09:01.600
<b>Let's crush the Revolutionary government
that framed us</b>

09:02.060 --> 09:07.270
<b>and bring to reality the new era
that Captain Sagara sought.</b>

09:11.030 --> 09:14.030
<b>RUROUNI KENSHIN</b>

09:16.200 --> 09:18.990
<b>Katsu, what are you planning?</b>

09:19.910 --> 09:24.410
<b>You ask what, but there is only one thing
that the Sekiho Army seeks.</b>

09:24.660 --> 09:26.830
<b>A new era with true equality
for the four classes</b>

09:26.830 --> 09:28.380
<b>that our captain dreamed of.</b>

09:28.750 --> 09:31.880
<b>I'm gonna crush the Meiji government
that's in the way.</b>

09:32.340 --> 09:35.800
<b>Don't tell me you don't remember
the recent Seinan War</b>

09:35.800 --> 09:37.840
<b>'cause you were drawing the whole time.</b>

09:38.300 --> 09:42.220
<b>Kagoshima, where Saigo raised his troops,
was at the edge of Japan.</b>

09:42.220 --> 09:45.770
<b>No matter how much you fight down there,
it's all in vain.</b>

09:45.980 --> 09:48.980
<b>My target is the center of Japan.</b>

09:48.980 --> 09:51.730
<b>By that, I mean this prefecture of Tokyo.</b>

09:52.150 --> 09:54.690
<b>The Home Ministry
oversees all domestic affairs.</b>

09:55.190 --> 09:58.990
<b>First off, we completely
shut its operation down.</b>

09:59.490 --> 10:03.330
<b>I'd like to crush the army, navy,
and the treasury at the same time as well,</b>

10:03.330 --> 10:05.250
<b>but I can't do all of that alone.</b>

10:05.250 --> 10:06.460
<b>Alone?</b>

10:06.460 --> 10:08.420
<b>I can't trust anyone else.</b>

10:08.920 --> 10:11.710
<b>I've been proceeding
with all of that by myself.</b>

10:11.710 --> 10:14.670
<b>Even though I'm alone,
I've still got these.</b>

10:15.760 --> 10:17.010
<b>Look at them, Sano.</b>

10:17.930 --> 10:21.550
<b>I made it with the knowledge of firearms
I gained in the Sekiho Army.</b>

10:21.760 --> 10:23.100
<b>They're bombs.</b>

10:23.890 --> 10:26.520
<b>I was cautious about not letting these
get traced back to me.</b>

10:26.520 --> 10:28.640
<b>It took me ten years to make these.</b>

10:28.640 --> 10:30.190
<b>I'm pretty confident about them.</b>

10:30.190 --> 10:33.230
<b>They explode and ignite fires,
so are efficient incendiary bombs.</b>

10:33.360 --> 10:36.150
<b>I will use these to blow up
all the ministries one after another</b>

10:36.150 --> 10:37.990
<b>to whittle away the centralized power,</b>

10:37.990 --> 10:41.320
<b>and then all the dissatisfied samurais
and farmers all over the country</b>

10:41.320 --> 10:43.330
<b>will naturally start rioting.</b>

10:43.830 --> 10:46.450
<b>The current government
is exhausted from the Seinan War,</b>

10:46.450 --> 10:48.120
<b>so they won't stand a chance.</b>

10:48.120 --> 10:51.540
<b>From there, I just need to wait for the
avalanche that will collapse everything.</b>

10:51.880 --> 10:56.130
<b>And afterwards, I will construct an era
where the four classes are truly equal</b>

10:56.130 --> 10:58.880
<b>and clear the names
of the Sekiho Army and its captain.</b>

11:00.840 --> 11:02.390
<b>I will execute my plan tomorrow...</b>

11:02.390 --> 11:05.100
<b>Sunday night,
when it will be the least populated.</b>

11:06.060 --> 11:09.060
<b>Sano, I don't mean to force this upon you.</b>

11:09.310 --> 11:11.190
<b>But I will go through it alone
if I have to,</b>

11:11.190 --> 11:13.980
<b>as a former member of the Sekiho Army.</b>

11:14.480 --> 11:16.860
<b>I'd like you to think about it
until sunset tomorrow</b>

11:16.860 --> 11:18.070
<b>and give me an answer then.</b>

11:24.450 --> 11:25.700
<b><i>It's impossible.</i></b>

11:26.200 --> 11:29.500
<b><i>Even if they're exhausted
from the Seinan War,</i></b>

11:29.500 --> 11:31.540
<b><i>the Meiji government isn't so weak</i></b>

11:31.540 --> 11:34.540
<b><i>that it would waver
from some explosions and sporadic riots.</i></b>

11:35.090 --> 11:37.460
<b><i>For the past 10 years,
he's only been thinking</i></b>

11:37.460 --> 11:40.880
<b><i>about clearing the name of the Sekiho Army
and our captain all by himself.</i></b>

11:41.340 --> 11:42.970
<b><i>He can't see the present.</i></b>

11:47.560 --> 11:50.060
<b>Ten years, huh?</b>

11:52.230 --> 11:53.350
<b>Damn it.</b>

11:54.480 --> 11:59.030
<b>It's already spring,
but the wind sure is cold.</b>

12:07.030 --> 12:07.870
<b>Sano?</b>

12:15.670 --> 12:16.630
<b>Captain...</b>

12:23.550 --> 12:24.930
<b>All right, it's fixed.</b>

12:25.510 --> 12:26.350
<b>Here.</b>

12:26.850 --> 12:28.100
<b>Thank you very much.</b>

12:28.600 --> 12:31.520
<b>When you're dealing with guns,
make sure to call for someone.</b>

12:31.520 --> 12:33.230
<b>Don't take them out without permission.</b>

12:33.640 --> 12:34.850
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

12:35.310 --> 12:38.900
<b>But you hit this well
with a warped barrel?</b>

12:39.400 --> 12:40.320
<b>That's some skill.</b>

12:40.820 --> 12:43.860
<b>I'm weak at swordsmanship
and physical strength,</b>

12:44.360 --> 12:46.070
<b>so I can at least do this.</b>

12:46.070 --> 12:47.490
<b>How promising.</b>

12:48.030 --> 12:50.370
<b>But you don't need to do that.</b>

12:50.370 --> 12:51.250
<b>Huh?</b>

12:51.500 --> 12:54.620
<b>Katsuhiro, you guys should study hard.</b>

12:54.830 --> 12:56.460
<b>Study, you say?</b>

12:56.960 --> 12:59.670
<b>The days of swords and guns will end soon.</b>

12:59.960 --> 13:03.260
<b>The next era will be that
of wits and knowledge.</b>

13:04.300 --> 13:06.090
<b>Those are your days.</b>

13:06.640 --> 13:08.970
<b>Meet more people,
and broaden your horizons.</b>

13:09.640 --> 13:12.600
<b>I'm letting you guys tag along
for that reason.</b>

13:12.600 --> 13:15.270
<b>But we... to protect you, Captain...</b>

13:15.940 --> 13:18.940
<b>I don't intend on surviving
by using you guys as my shields.</b>

13:19.860 --> 13:23.490
<b>Katsuhiro, you and Sanosuke
need to protect each other.</b>

13:23.820 --> 13:25.990
<b>Help each other, and head into the future.</b>

13:26.610 --> 13:28.910
<b>When times change,
so will the Sekiho Army.</b>

13:29.410 --> 13:32.200
<b>You guys will create the new Sekiho Army.</b>

13:33.950 --> 13:36.080
<b>I guess it's a bit
too difficult right now.</b>

13:36.870 --> 13:40.540
<b>But someday you will understand
what I am talking about.</b>

13:42.460 --> 13:46.970
<b>We... I could not protect you after all.</b>

13:47.470 --> 13:49.800
<b>And I couldn't get used
to the new era, either.</b>

13:50.600 --> 13:53.060
<b>But just you watch, Captain.</b>

13:54.020 --> 13:59.230
<b>My battle that I have poured
10 years into, my Sekiho Army...</b>

14:01.110 --> 14:03.860
<b>KAMIYA KASSHIN
SCHOOL OF KENDO</b>

14:04.110 --> 14:07.610
<b>Tsunan Tsukioka was an old friend
of yours, Sano, that he was?</b>

14:07.610 --> 14:10.320
<b>Those are some awkward
surprised faces you got there.</b>

14:10.320 --> 14:13.410
<b>Th-That's not necessarily true,
that it isn't. Right, Miss Kaoru?</b>

14:13.410 --> 14:15.080
<b>That's right, Kenshin!</b>

14:15.450 --> 14:16.580
<b>Oh, well.</b>

14:17.080 --> 14:20.670
<b>And so, to celebrate our reunion,
I thought about a big ol' party.</b>

14:21.130 --> 14:23.420
<b>Can you let me use the dojo tonight?</b>

14:24.000 --> 14:28.550
<b>I don't mind that, but where are you going
to get the money for a big old party?</b>

14:29.180 --> 14:31.600
<b>You're gonna leech off us again,
aren't you?</b>

14:31.600 --> 14:33.430
<b>I have to say no after all!
Absolutely not!</b>

14:33.430 --> 14:38.310
<b>You know, there's nothin' to worry about.
Leave the money bit to me.</b>

14:38.730 --> 14:40.400
<b>Well, I'm countin' on ya.</b>

14:41.060 --> 14:44.900
<b>Oh, right.
Invite Tae and the little girl, too.</b>

14:45.360 --> 14:47.190
<b>I'm pretty sure
they'd be happy about it.</b>

14:50.450 --> 14:51.450
<b>Strange.</b>

14:51.450 --> 14:52.780
<b>It's strange, all too strange!</b>

14:52.780 --> 14:55.290
<b>Maybe Sanosuke is sick somewhere? Right?</b>

14:55.790 --> 14:58.210
<b>C-Calm down, that you should.</b>

14:58.580 --> 15:00.920
<b>It is spring, after all...</b>

15:06.760 --> 15:08.220
<b>SAKE</b>

15:14.970 --> 15:17.470
<b>Then, let's get to it.</b>

15:17.470 --> 15:20.850
<b>So by "leave the money bit to me,"</b>

15:21.060 --> 15:23.400
<b>you meant you were going
to leech off Mr. Tsunan.</b>

15:23.900 --> 15:26.440
<b>It's not a big deal. Right?</b>

15:26.440 --> 15:27.570
<b>I don't care.</b>

15:27.690 --> 15:31.570
<b>I'm feeling sorry
that we're tagging along for all this.</b>

15:31.780 --> 15:33.410
<b>It's not a big deal.</b>

15:33.700 --> 15:35.530
<b>Well, if that's the case...</b>

15:35.530 --> 15:36.370
<b>Oh.</b>

15:38.750 --> 15:39.830
<b>She's here.</b>

15:40.330 --> 15:42.670
<b>I'm sorry. I...</b>

15:42.920 --> 15:45.670
<b>It's all right now. Right?</b>

15:45.880 --> 15:48.760
<b>If you're okay with it, Mr. Sano, we—</b>

15:48.760 --> 15:50.090
<b>Well, yeah.</b>

15:51.510 --> 15:57.390
<b>But Yoita loved gambling,
kids smiling, and women...</b>

15:57.720 --> 16:00.640
<b>so when you feel up to it,
please go visit his grave.</b>

16:00.770 --> 16:02.390
<b>She already did.</b>

16:02.560 --> 16:03.400
<b>Huh?</b>

16:03.730 --> 16:04.560
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

16:10.030 --> 16:12.860
<b>Mr. Sano, what kind of party is this?</b>

16:13.070 --> 16:16.160
<b>You treating us? This is a first.</b>

16:16.160 --> 16:18.290
<b>Don't worry about the details!</b>

16:18.410 --> 16:22.000
<b>Just drink and make some noise
'til you collapse!</b>

16:35.800 --> 16:40.270
<b>Well, I didn't know that Mr. Tsunan
was a childhood friend of Mr. Sano!</b>

16:40.270 --> 16:43.060
<b>What kind of kid was Mr. Sano?</b>

16:43.560 --> 16:44.520
<b>What kind?</b>

16:46.230 --> 16:47.190
<b>What is it?</b>

16:47.770 --> 16:49.070
<b>Not that different.</b>

16:49.610 --> 16:53.610
<b>Reckless, heading into things
without putting much thought into it.</b>

16:53.610 --> 16:55.490
<b>Man, that's so like Mr. Sano.</b>

16:55.990 --> 17:00.120
<b>And once he riots, he gets out of hand.
He's quite an explosive guy.</b>

17:00.330 --> 17:01.830
<b>Oh, just as I thought!</b>

17:01.830 --> 17:03.460
<b>I'll hang you, damn it!</b>

17:03.960 --> 17:04.830
<b>But...</b>

17:06.080 --> 17:09.040
<b>When push came to shove,
he was a reliable guy.</b>

17:17.340 --> 17:19.220
<b>Thank you very much!</b>

17:19.220 --> 17:20.760
<b>It will be a family heirloom!</b>

17:20.760 --> 17:23.980
<b>Th-Thank you so much.</b>

17:24.190 --> 17:25.020
<b>No need for thanks.</b>

17:25.440 --> 17:27.480
<b>You should get yourself drawn, too,
Mr. Sano.</b>

17:27.650 --> 17:30.650
<b>No, thanks.
He drew me tons when I was a kid.</b>

17:31.150 --> 17:34.490
<b>And I usually had a wound,
a lump, or a bruise.</b>

17:35.110 --> 17:36.320
<b>How pathetic.</b>

17:36.530 --> 17:39.200
<b>That was because you were
running around all the time.</b>

17:39.700 --> 17:41.580
<b>That's so Mr. Sano.</b>

17:41.580 --> 17:43.830
<b>Oh, then what about Mr. Himura?</b>

17:44.080 --> 17:46.540
<b>Oh, no, I—</b>

17:46.710 --> 17:48.670
<b>It's fine. He can draw you.</b>

17:48.670 --> 17:50.630
<b>It's just a game during a drinking party.</b>

17:50.840 --> 17:52.050
<b>Oro...</b>

17:54.920 --> 17:57.010
<b>How do you know Sanosuke?</b>

17:57.510 --> 17:58.680
<b>Just a friend, that he is.</b>

17:59.180 --> 18:00.970
<b>It all started with a slight scuffle.</b>

18:01.890 --> 18:03.430
<b>I heard you were a rurouni.</b>

18:04.310 --> 18:05.640
<b>What were you doing previously?</b>

18:06.640 --> 18:08.400
<b>I was over towards the west, that I was.</b>

18:10.110 --> 18:11.110
<b>Kyoto?</b>

18:14.940 --> 18:17.700
<b>Are you one of the Revolutionary warriors?</b>

18:20.280 --> 18:21.120
<b>Hey...</b>

18:22.080 --> 18:23.290
<b>That's right, that I was.</b>

18:26.790 --> 18:27.710
<b>I see.</b>

18:28.540 --> 18:31.840
<b>This is the first time I've drawn
an Imperialist who's right in front of me.</b>

18:31.840 --> 18:33.380
<b>Former, that is.</b>

18:33.880 --> 18:35.920
<b>I am just a rurouni now, that I am.</b>

18:36.420 --> 18:37.680
<b>Is that really so?</b>

18:39.890 --> 18:40.850
<b>I'm done.</b>

18:42.640 --> 18:44.640
<b>Oh, a man with no face?</b>

18:44.850 --> 18:46.680
<b>I draw what I see.</b>

18:47.270 --> 18:48.850
<b>I can't see this man.</b>

18:49.060 --> 18:54.070
<b>I can't see the face behind that smile,
what lies beyond that scar.</b>

18:59.070 --> 19:02.700
<b>Well, as long as we have this,
you can tell it's me, that you can.</b>

19:07.660 --> 19:09.750
<b>Mr. Sano, thanks for the meal!</b>

19:09.750 --> 19:12.210
<b>You show yourself at our place next time!</b>

19:12.210 --> 19:13.960
<b>Yeah, I'll do that.</b>

19:14.840 --> 19:16.420
<b>You guys be careful on your way home.</b>

19:16.920 --> 19:19.180
<b>I'm fully aware, Mr. Sano.</b>

19:19.180 --> 19:20.180
<b>See you again tomorrow!</b>

19:21.680 --> 19:22.800
<b>Yeah.</b>

19:22.800 --> 19:23.680
<b>See ya.</b>

19:34.980 --> 19:36.230
<b>Well...</b>

19:36.820 --> 19:38.940
<b>I guess it's about time to head out.</b>

19:39.400 --> 19:40.820
<b>That was your last supper.</b>

19:41.160 --> 19:43.120
<b>I hope you enjoyed it
to your heart's content.</b>

19:43.490 --> 19:44.620
<b>Not really.</b>

19:44.620 --> 19:47.290
<b>It wasn't a party I held
for a reason like that.</b>

19:47.500 --> 19:50.870
<b>Both Akabeko and missie
gave me quite a bit of food.</b>

19:51.540 --> 19:53.210
<b>So this is like saying thanks.</b>

19:53.750 --> 19:57.510
<b>SAKE</b>

19:53.960 --> 19:55.500
<b>Shu and Ginji were...</b>

19:55.500 --> 19:57.090
<b>you know, while I was at it.</b>

19:57.880 --> 19:59.470
<b>What about you?</b>

19:59.470 --> 20:00.800
<b>Did you have any fun?</b>

20:01.300 --> 20:03.090
<b>Hmph. Not at all.</b>

20:03.590 --> 20:06.260
<b>Really? You seemed to be talkin'
quite a bit.</b>

20:07.890 --> 20:09.730
<b>Is it really all right, Sanosuke?</b>

20:10.230 --> 20:14.100
<b>Idiot. I don't got
that stingy a personality.</b>

20:15.110 --> 20:16.110
<b>I see.</b>

20:17.230 --> 20:19.860
<b>How you chose the Sekiho Army
over the present</b>

20:19.860 --> 20:22.360
<b>is something I thank you for
from the bottom of my heart.</b>

20:24.660 --> 20:25.700
<b>Let's hurry.</b>

20:25.700 --> 20:27.910
<b>If we dilly-dally, the sun will rise.</b>

20:31.830 --> 20:33.420
<b>I'm sorry, guys.</b>

20:34.120 --> 20:36.130
<b>I won't ask you to understand.</b>

20:36.840 --> 20:40.170
<b>But the Sekiho Army
really is special to me.</b>

20:41.340 --> 20:47.300
<b>Kenshin, the next time I see you,
I'll be a felon for a grievous crime.</b>

20:47.720 --> 20:51.930
<b>I won't mind at all if you slay me
with that sakabato.</b>

22:44.960 --> 22:49.970
<b>NEXT EPISODE
TSUNAN & NISHIKI PAINTINGS</b>

22:46.420 --> 22:49.340
<b><i>Next episode,
"Tsunan & Nishiki Paintings."</i></b>
